Here is an example of a React component that implements autocomplete functionality without relying on other third-party packages:
```
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const Autocomplete = ({ data, value, onChange }) => {
  const [suggestions, setSuggestions] = useState([]);
  const [activeSuggestion, setActiveSuggestion] = useState(0);

  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchData = async (value) => {
      const filteredData = data.filter((item) => item.toLowerCase().includes(value.toLowerCase()));
      setSuggestions(filteredData);
    };

    if (value) {
      fetchData(value);
    }
  }, [value, data]);

  const handleInput = (event) => {
    const value = event.target.value;
    setActiveSuggestion(0);
    fetchData(value);
  };

  const handleSelect = (suggestion) => {
    onChange(suggestion);
    setActiveSuggestion(0);
  };

  const handleNavigate = (index) => {
    setActiveSuggestion(index);
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={value}
        onChange={handleInput}
        placeholder="Type to search..."
      />
      {suggestions.length > 0 && (
        <ul>
          {suggestions.map((suggestion, index) => (
            <li
              key={index}
              className={activeSuggestion === index ? 'active' : ''}
              onMouseDown={() => handleSelect(suggestion)}
            >
              {suggestion}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Autocomplete;
```
This component takes in three props:

* `data`: an array of suggestions to autocomplete
* `value`: the current value of the input field
* `onChange`: a function to call when the user selects a suggestion

The component uses two state variables: `suggestions` to store the filtered list of suggestions, and `activeSuggestion` to keep track of which suggestion is currently highlighted.

The component uses the `useEffect` hook to fetch the filtered list of suggestions whenever the value of the input field changes. It uses the `fetchData` function to filter the `data` array based on the current value of the input field.

The component also uses three event handlers:

* `handleInput`: updates the `value` prop and fetches the filtered list of suggestions when the user types in the input field
* `handleSelect`: calls the `onChange` function with the selected suggestion when the user selects a suggestion from the dropdown list
* `handleNavigate`: updates the `activeSuggestion` state variable when the user navigates to a different suggestion from the dropdown list

The component renders an input field and a list of suggestions. When the user types in the input field, the component fetches the filtered list of suggestions and updates the `suggestions` state variable. When the user selects a suggestion from the dropdown list, the component calls the `onChange` function and updates the `value` prop.

